<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Experiment Setup</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we outline the three tasks used to evaluate the TTT framework, along with the experimental setup.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Language Modeling </span>
We use the 760M parameter LaCT-LLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>)</cite> as our baseline model.
All models are trained on 100B tokens sampled from the FineWeb-Edu dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Penedo et al., 2024</a>)</cite>
with a batch size of 4 per GPU across 8 NVIDIA A100 GPUs for 20K iterations,
which takes approximately 56 hours to complete.
All other hyperparameters follow the original <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>)</cite> configuration.
For evaluation, we report perplexity on 2.5B tokens from the Book-3 dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2020</a>)</cite>.
All implementations are based on the Flame <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang and Yang, 2025</a>)</cite> codebase.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Novel View Synthesis </span>
We use 12-layer 768 hidden dimension LaCT-NVS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>)</cite> model as baseline, totaling 114M parameters.
We train our model on the RealEstate10K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2018</a>)</cite> dataset
with a batch size of 128 per GPU across 4 NVIDIA A100 GPUs for 20K iterations,
which takes approximately 38 hours to complete.
We use 2 input views and 6 target views for training, and 2 input views and 3 target views for evaluation.
All images are resized to <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128\times 128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>128</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128\times 128</annotation></semantics></math> resolution.
We train using only the MSE loss and evaluate using the Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio (PSNR) metric.
All other hyperparameters follow the original LaCT-NVS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>)</cite> configuration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Image Classification </span>
We use ViTTT-B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Han et al., 2025</a>)</cite> as our baseline model, totaling 90M parameters.
Follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Han et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, we train our model on the ImageNet-1K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al., 2009</a>)</cite> dataset
with a batch size of 256 per GPU across 2 NVIDIA H100 GPUs for 60 epochs,
which takes approximately 16 hours to complete.
We evaluate on the ImageNet-1K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al., 2009</a>)</cite> validation set using the top-1 accuracy.
All other hyperparameters follow the original <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Han et al., 2025</a>)</cite> configuration.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Linearization of Inner-Loop Updates). ‣ 5.1 General Form ‣ 5 TTT is secretly Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We explicitly unroll the single-step inner-loop update. Using the shorthand notation <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}(\cdot)\triangleq\phi(\cdot;\Theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}(\cdot)\triangleq\phi(\cdot;\Theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}(\cdot)\triangleq\phi_{t}(\cdot)W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}(\cdot)\triangleq\phi_{t}(\cdot)W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the model output for the key input <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> at step <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}(k)=\phi_{t}(k)\,W_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}(k)=\phi_{t}(k)\,W_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the chain rule, the gradient of the last layer with respect to the loss <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(k))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(k))</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{W_{t}}\mathcal{L}=\phi_{t}(k)^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W_{t}}\mathcal{L}=\phi_{t}(k)^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying one step of gradient descent with learning rate <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{t}-\eta\phi_{t}(k)^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{t}-\eta\phi_{t}(k)^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{t}+\phi_{t}(k)^{\top}g_{t}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{t}+\phi_{t}(k)^{\top}g_{t}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(k)\triangleq-\eta\,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{D_{\mathrm{out}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(k)\triangleq-\eta\,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{D_{\mathrm{out}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The kernel function parameters <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> are also updated with gradient descent, yielding the updated function <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t+1}(\cdot)=\phi(\cdot;\Theta_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t+1}(\cdot)=\phi(\cdot;\Theta_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Evaluating the updated model on a query <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle o</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q)\,W_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q)\,W_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q)\,\big(W_{t}+\phi_{t}(k)^{\top}g_{t}(k)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q)\,\big(W_{t}+\phi_{t}(k)^{\top}g_{t}(k)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">This expression is a linear attention operator of the form</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o=\hat{q}\left(S_{0}+\hat{k}^{\top}\hat{v}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=\hat{q}\left(S_{0}+\hat{k}^{\top}\hat{v}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}=\phi_{t+1}(q),\quad\hat{k}=\phi_{t}(k),\quad\hat{v}=g_{t}(k),\quad S_{0}=W_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}=\phi_{t+1}(q),\quad\hat{k}=\phi_{t}(k),\quad\hat{v}=g_{t}(k),\quad S_{0}=W_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Unrolling Inner-Loop Updates). ‣ 5.1 General Form ‣ 5 TTT is secretly Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove by induction on the number of tokens processed.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Base case.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Starting from initial parameters <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{0},\Theta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{0},\Theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, processing token <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> with key <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> applies one gradient descent step. By Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Linearization of Inner-Loop Updates). ‣ 5.1 General Form ‣ 5 TTT is secretly Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}=W_{0}+\phi_{0}(k_{0})^{\top}g_{0}(k_{0})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}=W_{0}+\phi_{0}(k_{0})^{\top}g_{0}(k_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{0}(k_{0})=-\eta\,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{0}(k_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{0}(k_{0})=-\eta\,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{0}(k_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is updated accordingly. This matches the claimed form with <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inductive step.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume that after processing tokens <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,\ldots,t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,\ldots,t-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}=W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t-1}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}g_{i}(k_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}=W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t-1}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}g_{i}(k_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Processing token <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> with key <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> applies another gradient descent step. By Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Linearization of Inner-Loop Updates). ‣ 5.1 General Form ‣ 5 TTT is secretly Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t+1}=W_{t}+\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}g_{t}(k_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t+1}=W_{t}+\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}g_{t}(k_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting the inductive hypothesis:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t+1}=W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t-1}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}g_{i}(k_{i})+\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}g_{t}(k_{t})=W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}g_{i}(k_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t+1}=W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t-1}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}g_{i}(k_{i})+\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}g_{t}(k_{t})=W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}g_{i}(k_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Output computation.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluating the model on query <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with the updated parameters gives:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle o_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle o_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\,W_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\,W_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\left(W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}g_{i}(k_{i})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\left(W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}g_{i}(k_{i})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This is the extended linear attention form:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}=\hat{q}_{t}\left(S_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\hat{k}_{i}^{\top}\hat{v}_{i}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}=\hat{q}_{t}\left(S_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\hat{k}_{i}^{\top}\hat{v}_{i}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{t}=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{t}=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{k}_{i}=\phi_{i}(k_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{k}_{i}=\phi_{i}(k_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{v}_{i}=g_{i}(k_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{v}_{i}=g_{i}(k_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}=W_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}=W_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 5.3 (Gradient Descent with Momentum). ‣ 5.1 General Form ‣ 5 TTT is secretly Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove by induction, extending the approach of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Unrolling Inner-Loop Updates). ‣ 5.1 General Form ‣ 5 TTT is secretly Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> to momentum updates.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Base case.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the momentum accumulator is initialized as <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{-1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{-1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="A4.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{0}=\nabla_{W}\mathcal{L}(f_{0}(k_{0}))=\phi_{0}(k_{0})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{0}(k_{0})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>W</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{0}=\nabla_{W}\mathcal{L}(f_{0}(k_{0}))=\phi_{0}(k_{0})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{0}(k_{0})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Applying the update rule <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}=W_{0}-\eta\Delta W_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}=W_{0}-\eta\Delta W_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A4.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}=W_{0}+\phi_{0}(k_{0})^{\top}g_{0}(k_{0})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}=W_{0}+\phi_{0}(k_{0})^{\top}g_{0}(k_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{0}(k_{0})=-\eta\,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{0}(k_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{0}(k_{0})=-\eta\,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{0}(k_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math>. This matches the claimed form with <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}(k_{0})=g_{0}(k_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}(k_{0})=g_{0}(k_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inductive step.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define the cumulative momentum coefficient from step <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> to step <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}^{j}\triangleq\begin{cases}\prod_{s=i+1}^{j}\alpha_{s}&amp;\text{if }i&lt;j,\\
1&amp;\text{if }i=j.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}^{j}\triangleq\begin{cases}\prod_{s=i+1}^{j}\alpha_{s}&amp;\text{if }i&lt;j,\\
1&amp;\text{if }i=j.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Assume that after processing tokens <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,\ldots,t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,\ldots,t-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the momentum accumulator satisfies</p>
<table id="A4.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{t-1}=\sum_{i=0}^{t-1}\beta_{i}^{t-1}\,\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{i}(k_{i})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{t-1}=\sum_{i=0}^{t-1}\beta_{i}^{t-1}\,\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{i}(k_{i})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">At step <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the momentum update gives</p>
<table id="A4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{W}\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(k_{t}))+\alpha_{t}\Delta W_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>W</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{W}\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(k_{t}))+\alpha_{t}\Delta W_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k_{t})}+\alpha_{t}\sum_{i=0}^{t-1}\beta_{i}^{t-1}\,\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{i}(k_{i})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k_{t})}+\alpha_{t}\sum_{i=0}^{t-1}\beta_{i}^{t-1}\,\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{i}(k_{i})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For terms <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[0,t-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[0,t-1]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\cdot\beta_{i}^{t-1}=\alpha_{t}\prod_{s=i+1}^{t-1}\alpha_{s}=\prod_{s=i+1}^{t}\alpha_{s}=\beta_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\cdot\beta_{i}^{t-1}=\alpha_{t}\prod_{s=i+1}^{t-1}\alpha_{s}=\prod_{s=i+1}^{t}\alpha_{s}=\beta_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=t</annotation></semantics></math> term, the coefficient is <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{t}=\sum_{i=0}^{t}\beta_{i}^{t}\,\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{i}(k_{i})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{t}=\sum_{i=0}^{t}\beta_{i}^{t}\,\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{i}(k_{i})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Weight accumulation.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{j+1}=W_{j}-\eta\Delta W_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{j+1}=W_{j}-\eta\Delta W_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t+1}=W_{0}-\eta\sum_{j=0}^{t}\Delta W_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t+1}=W_{0}-\eta\sum_{j=0}^{t}\Delta W_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting the closed form for <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and exchanging the order of summation:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{0}-\eta\sum_{j=0}^{t}\sum_{i=0}^{j}\beta_{i}^{j}\,\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{i}(k_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{0}-\eta\sum_{j=0}^{t}\sum_{i=0}^{j}\beta_{i}^{j}\,\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{i}(k_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}\underbrace{\left(-\eta\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{i}(k_{i})}\sum_{j=i}^{t}\beta_{i}^{j}\right)}_{m_{i}(k_{i})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}\underbrace{\left(-\eta\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{i}(k_{i})}\sum_{j=i}^{t}\beta_{i}^{j}\right)}_{m_{i}(k_{i})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The momentum-weighted effective value is thus</p>
<table id="A4.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}(k_{i})=g_{i}(k_{i})\cdot\sum_{j=i}^{t}\beta_{i}^{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}(k_{i})=g_{i}(k_{i})\cdot\sum_{j=i}^{t}\beta_{i}^{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Output computation.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluating the model on query <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with the updated parameters:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle o_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle o_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\,W_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\,W_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\left(W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}m_{i}(k_{i})\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\left(W_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}m_{i}(k_{i})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This is the linear attention form with <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{t}=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{t}=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{k}_{i}=\phi_{i}(k_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{k}_{i}=\phi_{i}(k_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{v}_{i}=m_{i}(k_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{v}_{i}=m_{i}(k_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}=W_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}=W_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Derivation: LaCT as Linear Attention</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the full derivation showing how LaCT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>)</cite> can be written in the form of linear attention, following the framework of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 5.3 (Gradient Descent with Momentum). ‣ 5.1 General Form ‣ 5 TTT is secretly Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>LaCT Architecture and Update Rule</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LaCT adopts a bias-free SwiGLU MLP as its inner-loop mapping:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=\bigl(\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0})\odot(xW_{2})\bigr)W_{1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>silu</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\bigl(\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0})\odot(xW_{2})\bigr)W_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0},W_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{D_{h}\times D_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0},W_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{D_{h}\times D_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{D_{h}\times D_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{D_{h}\times D_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The inner-loop objective uses the Frobenius inner product:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(f(k),v)=-\langle f(k),v\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(f(k),v)=-\langle f(k),v\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At each token <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, LaCT performs gradient descent with per-token learning rate <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, momentum <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and Muon-style <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jordan et al., 2024</a>)</cite> gradient orthogonalization <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{i,t}=\nabla_{W_{i,t}}\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(k_{t}),v_{t})+\alpha_{t}\Delta W_{i,t-1},\quad W_{i,t+1}=W_{i,t}-\eta_{t}\,\mathcal{M}(\Delta W_{i,t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{i,t}=\nabla_{W_{i,t}}\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(k_{t}),v_{t})+\alpha_{t}\Delta W_{i,t-1},\quad W_{i,t+1}=W_{i,t}-\eta_{t}\,\mathcal{M}(\Delta W_{i,t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Gradient Computation</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The upstream gradient with respect to the output is <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k_{t})}=-v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k_{t})}=-v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the chain rule, the gradient for the final layer <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{W_{1}}\mathcal{L}=\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k_{t})}=-\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}v_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W_{1}}\mathcal{L}=\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k_{t})}=-\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}v_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}(x)=\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0,t})\odot(xW_{2,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>silu</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}(x)=\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0,t})\odot(xW_{2,t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the kernel function.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Linear Attention Form with Muon</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the same induction as Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 5.3 (Gradient Descent with Momentum). ‣ 5.1 General Form ‣ 5 TTT is secretly Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>, but with the Muon orthogonalization <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> applied after each gradient accumulation, the weight update becomes:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1,t+1}=W_{1,0}-\sum_{j=0}^{t}\eta_{j}\,\mathcal{M}(\Delta W_{1,j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1,t+1}=W_{1,0}-\sum_{j=0}^{t}\eta_{j}\,\mathcal{M}(\Delta W_{1,j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using the cumulative momentum coefficient <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 5.3 (Gradient Descent with Momentum). ‣ 5.1 General Form ‣ 5 TTT is secretly Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>, the momentum accumulator for <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta W_{1,t}=-\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}v_{t}+\alpha_{t}\Delta W_{1,t-1}=-\sum_{i=0}^{t}\beta_{i}^{t}\,\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}v_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{1,t}=-\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}v_{t}+\alpha_{t}\Delta W_{1,t-1}=-\sum_{i=0}^{t}\beta_{i}^{t}\,\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}v_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting into the weight update and exchanging the order of summation (as in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 5.3 (Gradient Descent with Momentum). ‣ 5.1 General Form ‣ 5 TTT is secretly Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A5.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1,t+1}=W_{1,0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\mathcal{M}\!\left(\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}m_{i}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.031em;" width="1.031em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1,t+1}=W_{1,0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\mathcal{M}\!\left(\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}m_{i}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the momentum-weighted effective value is:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}\triangleq\eta_{i}\,v_{i}\cdot\sum_{j=i}^{t}\beta_{i}^{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}\triangleq\eta_{i}\,v_{i}\cdot\sum_{j=i}^{t}\beta_{i}^{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluating on query <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle o_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle o_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\,W_{1,t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\,W_{1,t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\left(W_{1,0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\mathcal{M}\!\left(\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}m_{i}\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.031em;" width="1.031em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\left(W_{1,0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\mathcal{M}\!\left(\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}m_{i}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This is a linear attention–like form where <math id="A5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}(k_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}(k_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> play the roles of keys and values, and <math id="A5.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> acts as the query. The Muon orthogonalization <math id="A5.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is applied element-wise to each key-value outer product before accumulation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Effect of Weight Normalization</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LaCT additionally applies weight normalization to <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> after each update:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1,t+1}=\mathrm{Norm}\!\left(W_{1,t}-\eta_{t}\,\mathcal{M}(\Delta W_{1,t})\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.584em;" width="2.584em"><mi>Norm</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1,t+1}=\mathrm{Norm}\!\left(W_{1,t}-\eta_{t}\,\mathcal{M}(\Delta W_{1,t})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Norm}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Norm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Norm}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> applies channel-wise <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> normalization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Weight normalization does <em id="A5.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> break the linear attention perspective. Recall that in the linear attention formulation, the state matrix <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=W_{1,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=W_{1,t}</annotation></semantics></math> accumulates key-value outer products. With weight normalization, we simply normalize this state after each update:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t+1}=\mathrm{Norm}\!\left(S_{t}+\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}m_{t}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.584em;" width="2.584em"><mi>Norm</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t+1}=\mathrm{Norm}\!\left(S_{t}+\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}m_{t}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The output remains a linear function of the (normalized) state:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\,S_{t+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\,S_{t+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, LaCT with weight normalization is still a linear attention mechanism—the query linearly reads from a state that accumulates key-value information.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, the normalization prevents expressing the state as a <em id="A5.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">simple sum</em> over history. Unlike the unnormalized case where <math id="A5.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t+1}=S_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t+1}=S_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi_{i}(k_{i})^{\top}m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the nested normalization creates a sequential dependency:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{Norm}\!\left(\mathrm{Norm}\!\left(S_{t-1}+\phi_{t-1}(k_{t-1})^{\top}m_{t-1}\right)+\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}m_{t}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.584em;" width="2.584em"><mi>Norm</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.584em;" width="2.584em"><mi>Norm</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{Norm}\!\left(\mathrm{Norm}\!\left(S_{t-1}+\phi_{t-1}(k_{t-1})^{\top}m_{t-1}\right)+\phi_{t}(k_{t})^{\top}m_{t}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This has implications for parallelization, which we discuss in Appendix <a href="#A9" title="Appendix I Non-Reducible Case Analysis ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Derivation: ViTTT GLU as Linear Attention</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show that the simplified GLU used in ViTTT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Han et al., 2025</a>)</cite> can be written into a linear attention form with element-wise multiplication.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Architecture and Loss</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In ViTTT, the GLU is defined as:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}(x)=\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0,t})\odot(xW_{1,t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>silu</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}(x)=\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0,t})\odot(xW_{1,t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0,t},W_{1,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{D_{h}\times D_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0,t},W_{1,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{D_{h}\times D_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> are both square matrices. We define the kernel function as</p>
<table id="A6.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}(x)\triangleq\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0,t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mi>silu</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}(x)\triangleq\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0,t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Unlike the general form where the kernel function output is followed by matrix multiplication with a final layer, here the GLU uses element-wise multiplication between the nonlinear gating <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and the linear projection <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="xW_{1,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">xW_{1,t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The inner-loop loss uses the Frobenius inner product:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(k_{t}),v_{t})=-\langle f_{t}(k_{t}),v_{t}\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(k_{t}),v_{t})=-\langle f_{t}(k_{t}),v_{t}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Gradient Computation</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The upstream gradient with respect to the GLU output is <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k_{t})}=-v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k_{t})}=-v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Applying the chain rule, the gradient of <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{W_{1,t}}\mathcal{L}=k_{t}^{\top}\left(\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k_{t})}\odot\phi_{t}(k_{t})\right)=-k_{t}^{\top}(v_{t}\odot\phi_{t}(k_{t}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W_{1,t}}\mathcal{L}=k_{t}^{\top}\left(\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(k_{t})}\odot\phi_{t}(k_{t})\right)=-k_{t}^{\top}(v_{t}\odot\phi_{t}(k_{t})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Linear Attention Form</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After one step of gradient descent with learning rate <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1,t+1}=W_{1,t}-\eta\nabla_{W_{1,t}}\mathcal{L}=W_{1,t}+\eta\,k_{t}^{\top}(v_{t}\odot\phi_{t}(k_{t}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1,t+1}=W_{1,t}-\eta\nabla_{W_{1,t}}\mathcal{L}=W_{1,t}+\eta\,k_{t}^{\top}(v_{t}\odot\phi_{t}(k_{t})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly, <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is updated to <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0,t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0,t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding the updated kernel function <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t+1}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t+1}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluating the model on query <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</p>
<table id="A6.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle o_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle o_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{t+1}(q_{t})=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\odot(q_{t}W_{1,t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{t+1}(q_{t})=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\odot(q_{t}W_{1,t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\odot\bigl(q_{t}W_{1,t}+\eta\,(q_{t}k_{t}^{\top})(v_{t}\odot\phi_{t}(k_{t}))\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\odot\bigl(q_{t}W_{1,t}+\eta\,(q_{t}k_{t}^{\top})(v_{t}\odot\phi_{t}(k_{t}))\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\odot\Bigl(q_{t}\bigl(W_{1,t}+k_{t}^{\top}(v_{t}\odot\phi_{t}(k_{t}))\bigr)\Bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})\odot\Bigl(q_{t}\bigl(W_{1,t}+k_{t}^{\top}(v_{t}\odot\phi_{t}(k_{t}))\bigr)\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This is a linear attention form where:</p>
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The second term computes a scalar attention weight <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle q_{t},k_{t}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle q_{t},k_{t}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> that modulates the value vector <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}(k_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}(k_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a multiplicative gate on the values</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t+1}(q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> gates the final output</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The state matrix <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=W_{1,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=W_{1,t}</annotation></semantics></math> accumulates outer products of keys and gated values, consistent with the general linear attention framework.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Derivation: ViTTT Depthwise Convolution as Linear Attention</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show that the <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> depthwise convolution layer in ViTTT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Han et al., 2025</a>)</cite> can be formulated as a form of spatially-local linear attention.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Architecture and Loss</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K,V\in\mathbb{R}^{C\times H\times W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K,V\in\mathbb{R}^{C\times H\times W}</annotation></semantics></math> be the spatial key and value tensors, and <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{C\times 1\times 3\times 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{C\times 1\times 3\times 3}</annotation></semantics></math> be the depthwise convolution weights at step <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
The forward pass computes:</p>
<table id="A7.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}(K)=\mathrm{Conv}_{3\times 3}(K;W_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Conv</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}(K)=\mathrm{Conv}_{3\times 3}(K;W_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Conv}_{3\times 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Conv</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Conv}_{3\times 3}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes depthwise convolution with <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> kernel.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The inner-loop loss uses the Frobenius inner product:</p>
<table id="A7.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(K),V)=-\langle f_{t}(K),V\rangle=-\sum_{c,i,j}[f_{t}(K)]_{c,i,j}\cdot V_{c,i,j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(K),V)=-\langle f_{t}(K),V\rangle=-\sum_{c,i,j}[f_{t}(K)]_{c,i,j}\cdot V_{c,i,j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Gradient Computation</h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The upstream gradient is <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(K)}=-V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(K)}=-V</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For depthwise convolution, the gradient with respect to the weight <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as:</p>
<table id="A7.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{W_{t}}\mathcal{L}=K\star\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(K)}=-K\star V," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W_{t}}\mathcal{L}=K\star\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(K)}=-K\star V,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\star" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋆</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\star</annotation></semantics></math> denotes cross-correlation. Specifically, for each channel <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> and offset <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\delta_{y},\delta_{x})\in\{-1,0,1\}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\delta_{y},\delta_{x})\in\{-1,0,1\}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A7.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\nabla_{W_{t}}\mathcal{L}]_{c,\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}=-\sum_{i,j}K_{c,i+\delta_{y},j+\delta_{x}}\cdot V_{c,i,j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\nabla_{W_{t}}\mathcal{L}]_{c,\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}=-\sum_{i,j}K_{c,i+\delta_{y},j+\delta_{x}}\cdot V_{c,i,j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3 </span>Linear Attention Form</h3>

<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After one step of gradient descent with learning rate <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A7.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[W_{t+1}]_{c,\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}=[W_{t}]_{c,\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}+\eta\sum_{i,j}K_{c,i+\delta_{y},j+\delta_{x}}\cdot V_{c,i,j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[W_{t+1}]_{c,\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}=[W_{t}]_{c,\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}+\eta\sum_{i,j}K_{c,i+\delta_{y},j+\delta_{x}}\cdot V_{c,i,j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When evaluating on query <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\in\mathbb{R}^{C\times H\times W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\in\mathbb{R}^{C\times H\times W}</annotation></semantics></math>, the output at position <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A7.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O_{c,i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O_{c,i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}[W_{t+1}]_{c,\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}\cdot Q_{c,i+\delta_{y},j+\delta_{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}[W_{t+1}]_{c,\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}\cdot Q_{c,i+\delta_{y},j+\delta_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\sum_{\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}[W_{t}]_{c,\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}\cdot Q_{c,i+\delta_{y},j+\delta_{x}}}_{[\mathrm{Conv}(Q;W_{t})]_{c,i,j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\sum_{\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}[W_{t}]_{c,\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}\cdot Q_{c,i+\delta_{y},j+\delta_{x}}}_{[\mathrm{Conv}(Q;W_{t})]_{c,i,j}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\eta\sum_{i^{\prime},j^{\prime}}\underbrace{\Big(\sum_{\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}Q_{c,i+\delta_{y},j+\delta_{x}}\cdot K_{c,i^{\prime}+\delta_{y},j^{\prime}+\delta_{x}}\Big)}_{\text{spatial attention weight}}\cdot V_{c,i^{\prime},j^{\prime}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>spatial attention weight</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\eta\sum_{i^{\prime},j^{\prime}}\underbrace{\Big(\sum_{\delta_{y},\delta_{x}}Q_{c,i+\delta_{y},j+\delta_{x}}\cdot K_{c,i^{\prime}+\delta_{y},j^{\prime}+\delta_{x}}\Big)}_{\text{spatial attention weight}}\cdot V_{c,i^{\prime},j^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This is a linear attention form where:</p>
<ul id="A7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The first term corresponds to the initial state <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}=W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}=W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The attention weight between query position <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> and key position <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is the sum of element-wise products over the <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> neighborhood offsets</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This spatially-local attention allows each output position to attend to all key-value positions, weighted by the overlap of their local <math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> neighborhoods</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Conceptually, since convolution is effectively a sliding-window linear layer, this TTT component is equivalent to a sliding-window linear attention mechanism.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Parallel Form of TTT</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present the parallel formulation for TTT when only <math id="A8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is dynamic (while <math id="A8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are static) and weight normalization is omitted. Under these conditions, the kernel function becomes static:</p>
<table id="A8.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)=\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0})\odot(xW_{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>silu</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)=\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0})\odot(xW_{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the state update is associative, enabling parallel computation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.1 </span>Parallel Formulation</h3>

<div id="A8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The parallel formulation operates on a sequence of <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> chunks, each of size <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q},\mathbb{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{(NL)\times D_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕂</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q},\mathbb{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{(NL)\times D_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{(NL)\times D_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{(NL)\times D_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the concatenated query, key, and value inputs across all chunks. Define the batched kernel function:</p>
<table id="A8.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(\mathbf{X})=\mathrm{silu}(\mathbf{X}W_{0})\odot(\mathbf{X}W_{2})\in\mathbb{R}^{(NL)\times D_{h}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>silu</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\mathbf{X})=\mathrm{silu}(\mathbf{X}W_{0})\odot(\mathbf{X}W_{2})\in\mathbb{R}^{(NL)\times D_{h}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To express chunk-wise operations, we introduce:</p>
<ul id="A8.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Block-diagonal matrix <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{(NL)\times(NL)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{(NL)\times(NL)}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}=\mathrm{diag}(I_{L},\ldots,I_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}=\mathrm{diag}(I_{L},\ldots,I_{L})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> identity blocks</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Learning rate vector <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\eta}\in\mathbb{R}^{(NL)\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜼</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\eta}\in\mathbb{R}^{(NL)\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>: per-token learning rates</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Scaled values <math id="A8.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{V}}=\mathbb{V}\odot\boldsymbol{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝜼</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{V}}=\mathbb{V}\odot\boldsymbol{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Momentum matrix <math id="A8.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A8.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{ij}=\prod_{s=j+1}^{i}\alpha_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{ij}=\prod_{s=j+1}^{i}\alpha_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A8.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq j</annotation></semantics></math>, else <math id="A8.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Causal mask <math id="A8.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}\in\{0,1\}^{N\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}\in\{0,1\}^{N\times N}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A8.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{ij}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{ij}=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A8.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq j</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The output can be computed in parallel as:</p>
<table id="A8.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{O}=\Phi(\mathbb{Q})\,W_{1,0}+\big((\Phi(\mathbb{Q})\,\Phi(\mathbb{K})^{\top})\odot(\mathcal{A}\odot\mathbf{M})^{\uparrow L}\big)\,\tilde{\mathbb{V}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕆</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}=\Phi(\mathbb{Q})\,W_{1,0}+\big((\Phi(\mathbb{Q})\,\Phi(\mathbb{K})^{\top})\odot(\mathcal{A}\odot\mathbf{M})^{\uparrow L}\big)\,\tilde{\mathbb{V}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\cdot)^{\uparrow L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\cdot)^{\uparrow L}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Kronecker product with <math id="A8.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{L\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{L\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> to expand the <math id="A8.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\times N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\times N</annotation></semantics></math> mask to <math id="A8.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(NL)\times(NL)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(NL)\times(NL)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.2 </span>Proof of Equivalence</h3>

<div id="A8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prove that this parallel formulation is equivalent to the sequential recurrence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the sequential formulation where at each chunk <math id="A8.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the weight update is:</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{t}=\nabla_{W_{1}}\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(K_{t}))+\alpha_{t}\Delta W_{t-1},\quad W_{1,t+1}=W_{1,t}-\eta_{t}\Delta W_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{t}=\nabla_{W_{1}}\mathcal{L}(f_{t}(K_{t}))+\alpha_{t}\Delta W_{t-1},\quad W_{1,t+1}=W_{1,t}-\eta_{t}\Delta W_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A8.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{W_{1}}\mathcal{L}=\Phi(K_{t})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(K_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W_{1}}\mathcal{L}=\Phi(K_{t})^{\top}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(K_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math> and using the Frobenius inner product loss, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{t}=-\Phi(K_{t})^{\top}V_{t}+\alpha_{t}\Delta W_{t-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{t}=-\Phi(K_{t})^{\top}V_{t}+\alpha_{t}\Delta W_{t-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Unroll the momentum recurrence.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Expanding <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A8.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex90.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{i=0}^{t}\left(\prod_{s=i+1}^{t}\alpha_{s}\right)\Phi(K_{i})^{\top}V_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{i=0}^{t}\left(\prod_{s=i+1}^{t}\alpha_{s}\right)\Phi(K_{i})^{\top}V_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Unroll the weight recurrence.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1,t+1}=W_{1,0}-\sum_{j=0}^{t}\eta_{j}\Delta W_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1,t+1}=W_{1,0}-\sum_{j=0}^{t}\eta_{j}\Delta W_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, substituting and rearranging:</p>
<table id="A8.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1,t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1,t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex91.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{1,0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\Phi(K_{i})^{\top}V_{i}\cdot\underbrace{\eta_{i}\sum_{j=i}^{t}\left(\prod_{s=i+1}^{j}\alpha_{s}\right)}_{c_{i}^{t}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{1,0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\Phi(K_{i})^{\top}V_{i}\cdot\underbrace{\eta_{i}\sum_{j=i}^{t}\left(\prod_{s=i+1}^{j}\alpha_{s}\right)}_{c_{i}^{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Compute the sequential output.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The output at chunk <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A8.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex92.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Phi(Q_{t})\,W_{1,t+1}=\Phi(Q_{t})\,W_{1,0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\Phi(Q_{t})\,\Phi(K_{i})^{\top}V_{i}\cdot c_{i}^{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Phi(Q_{t})\,W_{1,t+1}=\Phi(Q_{t})\,W_{1,0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\Phi(Q_{t})\,\Phi(K_{i})^{\top}V_{i}\cdot c_{i}^{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 4: Match with parallel formulation.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The mask <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{A}\odot\mathbf{M})^{\uparrow L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{A}\odot\mathbf{M})^{\uparrow L}</annotation></semantics></math> at block <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t,i)</annotation></semantics></math> has value <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=i}^{t}\prod_{s=i+1}^{j}\alpha_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=i}^{t}\prod_{s=i+1}^{j}\alpha_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq t</annotation></semantics></math>. The parallel form computes:</p>
<table id="A8.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[\mathbb{O}]_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝕆</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\mathbb{O}]_{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex93.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Phi(Q_{t})_{p}\,W_{1,0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\Phi(Q_{t})_{p}\,\Phi(K_{i})^{\top}V_{i}\cdot c_{i}^{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Phi(Q_{t})_{p}\,W_{1,0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\Phi(Q_{t})_{p}\,\Phi(K_{i})^{\top}V_{i}\cdot c_{i}^{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which exactly matches the sequential output.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Non-Reducible Case Analysis</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S6.SS2" title="6.2 Parallel Form of TTT ‣ 6 Practical Implications ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a>, we showed that TTT becomes reducible (and thus parallelizable) when only <math id="A9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is dynamic while <math id="A9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are static.
Here, we analyze two cases that break reducibility: (1) updating the kernel function parameters <math id="A9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta=\{W_{0},W_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta=\{W_{0},W_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and (2) applying weight normalization.</p>
</div>
<section id="A9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.1 </span>Case 1: Dynamic Kernel Function (Updating <math id="A9.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.SS1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h3>

<div id="A9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are also updated, the kernel function <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}(x)=\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0,t})\odot(xW_{2,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>silu</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}(x)=\mathrm{silu}(xW_{0,t})\odot(xW_{2,t})</annotation></semantics></math> becomes history-dependent.
Consider the gradient update for <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (the analysis for <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is analogous):</p>
<table id="A9.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{W_{0,t}}\mathcal{L}=K_{t}^{\top}\Big(\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(K_{t})}W_{1,t}^{\top}\odot(K_{t}W_{2,t})\odot\operatorname{silu}^{\prime}(K_{t}W_{0,t})\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><msup><mi>silu</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W_{0,t}}\mathcal{L}=K_{t}^{\top}\Big(\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{t}(K_{t})}W_{1,t}^{\top}\odot(K_{t}W_{2,t})\odot\operatorname{silu}^{\prime}(K_{t}W_{0,t})\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The weight update becomes:</p>
<table id="A9.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0,t+1}=W_{0,t}-\eta_{t}\nabla_{W_{0,t}}\mathcal{L}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0,t+1}=W_{0,t}-\eta_{t}\nabla_{W_{0,t}}\mathcal{L}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Expanding recursively, the kernel function at step <math id="A9.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="A9.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0,t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A9.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}(K_{t})=\operatorname{silu}(K_{t}W_{0,t})\odot(K_{t}W_{2,t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>silu</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}(K_{t})=\operatorname{silu}(K_{t}W_{0,t})\odot(K_{t}W_{2,t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting the recursive expression for <math id="A9.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0,t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the kernel function involves nested nonlinearities:</p>
<table id="A9.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}(K_{t})=\operatorname{silu}\Big(K_{t}\big(W_{0,t-1}-\eta_{t-1}\nabla_{W_{0,t-1}}\mathcal{L}\big)\Big)\odot(\cdots)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>silu</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}(K_{t})=\operatorname{silu}\Big(K_{t}\big(W_{0,t-1}-\eta_{t-1}\nabla_{W_{0,t-1}}\mathcal{L}\big)\Big)\odot(\cdots),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A9.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{W_{0,t-1}}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W_{0,t-1}}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> itself contains <math id="A9.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{silu}^{\prime}(K_{t-1}W_{0,t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>silu</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{silu}^{\prime}(K_{t-1}W_{0,t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The nested <math id="A9.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{silu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>silu</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{silu}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{silu}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>silu</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{silu}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> functions create a non-linear dependency chain: computing <math id="A9.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> requires <math id="A9.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0,t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which depends on <math id="A9.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{silu}^{\prime}(K_{t-1}W_{0,t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>silu</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{silu}^{\prime}(K_{t-1}W_{0,t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, which in turn depends on <math id="A9.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0,t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0,t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and so on. This nested structure prevents expressing the output as a simple weighted sum over history, breaking the associativity required for parallel prefix scan.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.2 </span>Case 2: Weight Normalization</h3>

<div id="A9.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Even when only <math id="A9.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is dynamic, applying weight normalization (as in LaCT, see Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Derivation: LaCT as Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>) introduces non-reducibility for the parallel formulation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Derivation: LaCT as Linear Attention ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>, weight normalization does not break the linear attention <em id="A9.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">interpretation</em>—it simply normalizes the state <math id="A9.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> after each token. However, it does prevent the <em id="A9.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">parallel computation</em> enabled by the sum form.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The key issue is that normalization is not associative:</p>
<table id="A9.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Norm}(A+B)\neq\text{Norm}(A)+\text{Norm}(B)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Norm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Norm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Norm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Norm}(A+B)\neq\text{Norm}(A)+\text{Norm}(B).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The parallel formulation in Section <a href="#S6.SS2" title="6.2 Parallel Form of TTT ‣ 6 Practical Implications ‣ Test-Time Training with KV Binding Is Secretly Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a> relies on expressing the state as <math id="A9.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t+1}=S_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi(K_{i})^{\top}m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t+1}=S_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{t}\phi(K_{i})^{\top}m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be computed via associative parallel prefix scan. With weight normalization, the state becomes:</p>
<table id="A9.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t+1}=\mathrm{Norm}\Big(\mathrm{Norm}(S_{t-1}+\phi(K_{t-1})^{\top}m_{t-1})+\phi(K_{t})^{\top}m_{t}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Norm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Norm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t+1}=\mathrm{Norm}\Big(\mathrm{Norm}(S_{t-1}+\phi(K_{t-1})^{\top}m_{t-1})+\phi(K_{t})^{\top}m_{t}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This nested structure creates a strict sequential dependency: computing <math id="A9.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> requires the fully normalized <math id="A9.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which requires <math id="A9.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and so on. The associativity required for parallel prefix scan is broken, forcing token-by-token sequential computation even though the underlying mechanism remains linear attention.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
